title: Inter-Party Relationships
new-page: true
view-if: year <= 1932 and inter_party_relationships_timer <= 0
tags: party_affairs
is-card: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; inter_party_relationships_timer = 6;
card-image: img/kcp_interparty_relations.png
#subtitle: Building relations with the other political parties of Kadja.

= Inter-Party Relationships

The KCP can often govern on its own however it would always be good to build relations with the other parties just in case.

- @liberals: Try to build warm relations with the Peoples Front.
- @center: Try to fix the rift with the Unitarists
- @spd_alone: The KCP can stand alone for now.
- @easy_discard


@center
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; up_relation += 2 if up_party_leader == "Moriarty"
go-to: left_coalition if kcp_in_government = 1 and up_in_government = 1


@left_coalition
on-arrival: z_relation += 8*(1 - dissent)

We are currently coalition partners with them, so improving relations comes naturally.

@liberals
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; vnpf_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)
go-to: yoakumaen_vnpf if yoakumaen_adopted = 1; traditional_vnpf if traditional_adopted = 1

The VNPF has never been our ally or even perceived friend and many comments we made about them have been seen as provocative and hostile. But we can still try to fix relations.

@yoakumaen_vnpf
on-arrival: vnpf_relation += 2*(1 - dissent)

With the adoption of the Yoakumaen reconstruction plan the VNPF is greatly more hostile towards us than before as they see it as undermining their local culture and the very base of their support.

@traditional_vnpf
on-arrival: vnpf_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

With our adoption of the traditional reconstruction plan we have been able to greatly ease relations between our two parties to a point where even a coalition might be possible.


@spd_alone

Whether it is because we *cannot* or *will not*, we do not make ties with other parties at this moment.

- @return: Continue...
